data: {"type": "tool_result", "id": "c1", "iteration": 1, "name": "search_my_history", "result": {"matches": [{"title": "Obsession", "year": "2025", "confidence": 0.515, "text": "Obsession (2025)\nDaisy is perfect. Ramona is not perfect. Therefore, Daisy must watch Ramona. Daisy must follow Ramona. Daisy must perfect Ramona.\nTone: Unsettlingly intimate and deeply fixated, suffused with a dark, compulsive tension that breeds a persistent psychological dread.\nTone: Unsettlingly intimate and deeply fixated, suffused with a dark, compulsive tension that breeds a persistent psychological dread.\nMy take: Made me uneasy in a good way\nMy take: Made me uneasy in a good way\nMy take: Made me uneasy in a good way"}, {"title": "Companion", "year": "2025", "confidence": 0.101, "text": "Companion (2025)\nDuring a weekend getaway at a secluded lakeside estate, a group of friends finds themselves entangled in a web of secrets, deception, and advanced technology. As tensions rise and loyalties are tested, they uncover unsettling truths about themselves and the world around them.\nThemes: android, artificial intelligence (a.i.), cabin, robot, boyfriend girlfriend relationship, duringcreditsstinger, robot girl, weekend getaway, human android relationship, toxic relationship\nTone: Tense, paranoid, and deeply unsettling, leaving a chilling sense of claustrophobic dread and sinister psychological manipulation.\nTone: Tense, paranoid, and deeply unsettling, leaving a chilling sense of claustrophobic dread and sinister psychological manipulation."}, {"title": "Us", "year": "2019", "confidence": 0.047, "text": "Us (2019)\nHusband and wife Gabe and Adelaide Wilson take their kids to their beach house expecting to unplug and unwind with friends. But as night descends, their serenity turns to tension and chaos when some shocking visitors arrive uninvited.\nThemes: mask, boardwalk, murder, psychological thriller, fear, family vacation, home invasion, amusement park, doppelg\u00e4nger, santa cruz, california\nTone: Tense, aggressive, and deeply unsettling, driven by a creeping sense of paranoia and disturbing, ambiguous dread.\nTone: Tense, aggressive, and deeply unsettling, driven by a creeping sense of paranoia and disturbing, ambiguous dread.\nMy take: Such a unique concept\nMy take: Such a unique concept\nMy take: Such a unique concept"}, {"title": "Together", "year": "2025", "confidence": 0.042, "text": "Together (2025)\nYears into their relationship, Tim and Millie find themselves at a crossroads as they move to the country, abandoning all that is familiar in their lives except each other. With tensions already flaring, a nightmarish encounter with a mysterious, unnatural force threatens to corrupt their lives, their love, and their flesh.\nThemes: countryside, musician, cave, cult, woods, romance, teacher, church, couple, psychotic\nTone: Suffocating and emotionally raw, combining intimate romantic paranoia with a grotesque, deeply unsettling sense of visceral dread.\nTone: Suffocating and emotionally raw, combining intimate romantic paranoia with a grotesque, deeply unsettling sense of visceral dread."}, {"title": "Parasite", "year": "2019", "confidence": 0.032, "text": "Parasite (2019)\nAll unemployed, Ki-taek's family takes peculiar interest in the wealthy and glamorous Parks for their livelihood until they get entangled in an unexpected incident.\nThemes: dark comedy, con artist, social commentary, working class, infiltration, psychological thriller, class differences, family, unemployed, domestic worker\nTone: Tense, darkly hilarious, and profoundly unsettling, building a suffocating mood of escalating anxiety, cynicism, and heartbreaking dread.\nTone: Tense, darkly hilarious, and profoundly unsettling, building a suffocating mood of escalating anxiety, cynicism, and heartbreaking dread."}, {"title": "Get Out", "year": "2017", "confidence": 0.016, "text": "Get Out (2017)\nChris and his girlfriend Rose go upstate to visit her parents for the weekend. At first, Chris reads the family's overly accommodating behavior as nervous attempts to deal with their daughter's interracial relationship, but as the weekend progresses, a series of increasingly disturbing discoveries lead him to a truth that he never could have imagined.\nThemes: kidnapping, externally controlled action, manipulation, dark comedy, hypnosis, parents-in-law, satire, racist, revenge, interracial relationship\nTone: Intensely paranoid and deeply unsettling, blending a creeping sense of dread with sharp, darkly satirical anxiety.\nTone: Intensely paranoid and deeply unsettling, blending a creeping sense of dread with sharp, darkly satirical anxiety."}, {"title": "Doctor Strange in the Multiverse of Madness", "year": "2022", "confidence": 0.014, "text": "Doctor Strange in the Multiverse of Madness (2022)\nDoctor Strange, with the help of mystical allies both old and new, traverses the mind-bending and dangerous alternate realities of the Multiverse to confront a mysterious new adversary.\nThemes: magic, superhero, based on comic, alternative reality, aftercreditsstinger, duringcreditsstinger, marvel cinematic universe (mcu)\nTone: Darkly chaotic and macabre, steeped in desperate grief with a pervasive sense of surreal, unsettling dread.\nTone: Darkly chaotic and macabre, steeped in desperate grief with a pervasive sense of surreal, unsettling dread."}, {"title": "Training Day", "year": "2001", "confidence": 0.014, "text": "Training Day (2001)\nOn his first day on the job as a narcotics officer, a rookie cop works with a rogue detective who isn't what he appears.\nThemes: drug dealer, california, police brutality, poker, bratva (russian mafia), war on drugs, drug trafficking, police corruption, los angeles, california, gang member\nTone: Gritty, volatile, and deeply cynical, radiating an unpredictable predatory tension that leaves you feeling breathless and unsettled.\nTone: Gritty, volatile, and deeply cynical, radiating an unpredictable predatory tension that leaves you feeling breathless and unsettled.\nMy take: First Denzel movie I\u2019ve seen he\u2019s so good\nMy take: First Denzel movie I\u2019ve seen he\u2019s so good\nMy take: First Denzel movie I\u2019ve seen he\u2019s so good"}]}, "blocked_duplicate": false, "duration_ms": 1828}

event: answer
data: {"type": "answer", "text": "Here are the films from your watch history that carry an uneasy or unsettling mood:\n\n* **Obsession (2025)** \u2013 Centered on a dark, compulsive fixation and stalking, this psychological thriller has a deeply unsettling tone. Your review explicitly noted it *\"made me uneasy in a good way.\"*\n* **Companion (2025)** \u2013 A tense thriller about a weekend getaway involving advanced technology, deception, and psychological manipulation, creating a paranoid and claustrophobic sense of dread.\n* **Us (2019)** \u2013 Jordan Peele's thriller about a family confronted by sinister doppelg\u00e4ngers, filled with creeping paranoia and disturbing, ambiguous dread.\n* **Together (2025)** \u2013 A intimate horror/thriller following a couple whose move to the countryside leads to a nightmarish encounter with a grotesque force, combining romantic tension with visceral dread.\n* **Parasite (2019)** \u2013 A dark, satirical thriller about class division and infiltration that builds an escalating mood of anxiety, tension, and unsettling dread.\n* **Get Out (2017)** \u2013 A psychological horror film that uses disturbing discoveries during a family visit to create an intensely paranoid, deeply unsettling atmosphere.", "iteration": 2, "films": [{"tmdb_id": 1436161, "title": "Obsession", "year": 2025, "watched": true, "my_rating": 4.5, "vote_average": 0.0, "poster_url": null, "overview": "Daisy is perfect. Ramona is not perfect. Therefore, Daisy must watch Ramona. Daisy must follow Ramona. Daisy must perfect Ramona."}, {"tmdb_id": 1084199, "title": "Companion", "year": 2025, "watched": true, "my_rating": 3.5, "vote_average": 7.004, "poster_url": "https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/oCoTgC3UyWGfyQ9thE10ulWR7bn.jpg", "overview": "During a weekend getaway at a secluded lakeside estate, a group of friends finds themselves entangled in a web of secrets, deception, and advanced technology. As tensions rise and loyalties are tested, they uncover unsettling truths about themselves and the world around them."}, {"tmdb_id": 458723, "title": "Us", "year": 2019, "watched": true, "my_rating": 4.0, "vote_average": 6.9, "poster_url": "https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/ux2dU1jQ2ACIMShzB3yP93Udpzc.jpg", "overview": "Husband and wife Gabe and Adelaide Wilson take their kids to their beach house expecting to unplug and unwind with friends. But as night descends, their serenity turns to tension and chaos when some shocking visitors arrive uninvited."}, {"tmdb_id": 1242011, "title": "Together", "year": 2025, "watched": true, "my_rating": 3.5, "vote_average": 6.904, "poster_url": "https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/80slKYVM5teFH3kz6ouWrZXveqj.jpg", "overview": "Years into their relationship, Tim and Millie find themselves at a crossroads as they move to the country, abandoning all that is familiar in their lives except each other. With tensions already flaring, a nightmarish encounter with a mysterious, unnatural force threatens to corrupt their lives, their love, and their flesh."}, {"tmdb_id": 496243, "title": "Parasite", "year": 2019, "watched": true, "my_rating": 5.0, "vote_average": 8.49, "poster_url": "https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/7IiTTgloJzvGI1TAYymCfbfl3vT.jpg", "overview": "All unemployed, Ki-taek's family takes peculiar interest in the wealthy and glamorous Parks for their livelihood until they get entangled in an unexpected incident."}, {"tmdb_id": 419430, "title": "Get Out", "year": 2017, "watched": true, "my_rating": 5.0, "vote_average": 7.625, "poster_url": "https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/tFXcEccSQMf3lfhfXKSU9iRBpa3.jpg", "overview": "Chris and his girlfriend Rose go upstate to visit her parents for the weekend. At first, Chris reads the family's overly accommodating behavior as nervous attempts to deal with their daughter's interracial relationship, but as the weekend progresses, a series of increasingly disturbing discoveries lead him to a truth that he never could have imagined."}]}

